--- Completion 3 ---
To calculate the number of laptops present in the image, I will use the "pixel_level_depth_estimator" tool. This tool can help us estimate the depth map of an image. By filtering the depth map, we can identify the positions of objects, which might correspond to laptops. The tool can take into account image brightness and color information to assist in this task. As a tool, the following Python code extracts and processes the depth map of an image to estimate its depth level:

<command>
import numpy as np
import cv2

def depth_estimate(image, outdir='./'):
    # Estimate depth from an image
    depth_img = cv2.imread(image, 0)
    depth_img = np.log2(depth_img)
    depth_img = np.abs(depth_img)
    depth_img = np.mean(depth_img, axis=2, keepdims=True)

    # Find contours and apply filtering
    contours, _ = cv2.findContours(depth_img, cv2.RETR_EXTERNAL, cv2.CHAIN_APPROX_SIMPLE)
    contours = [c for c in contours if c.shape[0] > 200]

    # Check depth for each contour
    for contour in contours:
        x0, y0, x1, y1 = cv2.boundingRect(contour)
        depth = np.max(np.abs(depth_img[y0:y1, x0:x1]))

        # Check for enough pixels
        if depth < 5 and np.count_nonzero(depth >= 5) > 1000:
            print("# Detected a laptop at ( {:.5f}, {:.5f} ).".format(x0 + 20 * np.cos(np.pi/60), y0 + 20 * np.sin(np.pi/60)))

# Example usage
depth_estimate('/path/to/image.png', outdir='./visualizations')
</command>

请确保将'/path/to/image.png'替换为实际的图像路径。该功能尝试识别红色物体，并在不需要识别红色物体时手动添加，然后检查每个像素的深度（基于图像的亮度/颜色），记住只有超过一定的深度量值时才能初步确认为红色物体。这个过程会依据深度量值来识别物体。您可以根据需要自定义这个判断过程（例如，考虑自定义深度阈值等）。
